## Patch and evidence

- `tests/perf/windows_process_metrics.py`: add `GetExitCodeProcess` binding and checked `poll_exit_code()`. A signaled handle establishes termination; wait failure, unexpected wait, missing handle and exit-query failure raise errors. Terminal DWORD values, including 259 and crash codes, are preserved. Existing `alive()`, sampling and Job cleanup behavior stay compatible.
- `tests/e2e/runner.py`: require terminal exit zero before accepting observations and retain `adapter_exit_code` before cleanup. Null means no terminal outcome was established. The evidence importer also requires integer zero, rejecting legacy results without exit status and Boolean/string substitutes. The separate xtask result format is unchanged.
- `tests/e2e/test_adapter_exit.py` and `test_runner.py`: focused regressions cover the failure boundaries and success path. The README documents the stricter evidence contract; older native runner results lacking the field require recapture.
- [Retained evidence and commands](../../qa/2026-09-15-dev001-adapter-exit/README.md): 27 focused tests, exit-7 FAIL/1, exit-0 PASS/0 and Windows parent/descendant cleanup. Source hashes identify the tested local patch at baseline HEAD `e6c1486ff0bb997d96801331b32986d612728d4f`.

